// TYPECHECK-ONLY PROJECT — wider than the build, emits nothing.
//
// `tsconfig.json` sets `rootDir:./src` because that is what the build emits, which means
// `scripts/` can never belong to it: adding it there is a TS6059 error, not an option. So the
// operational harnesses under `scripts/` were typechecked by NOTHING.
//
// That is not a hygiene point. `scripts/wp4-load-harness.ts` is the only executable evidence in
// the tree at 50,000-row scale, and it had been broken since M9 round 2 — its seeds set no `leg`,
// so the `validateNewClaim` check added that round made it throw at seed time. It sat outside
// `include`, so `npm run typecheck` never saw it, and two full rounds of "verification" ran with
// the one harness that could have produced scale evidence silently dead. Defect  had no
// natural home because of it.
//
// This project exists so that can never recur: same compiler options, no emit, `scripts/` in
// scope. `npm run typecheck` points here. The build still uses `tsconfig.json` untouched.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    // The build pins rootDir to./src to shape `dist/`. Nothing is emitted here, so the wider
    // root is free — and is what lets `scripts/` be checked at all.
    "rootDir": "."
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "scripts/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "src/**/*.test.ts"]
}
